      "Language": "fre",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "We report the case of a patient who was admitted for acute coronary syndrom associated with fever originating from urinary tract. Coronary arteriography revealed a huge coronary aneurysm which ruptured a short time after diagnosis. After surgery, it was proven to be mycotic aneurysm related to Escherichia Coli sepsis."},
